WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:03.400
-Democrats will retain
control of the Senate

00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:04.467
after news organizations

00:00:04.467 --> 00:00:06.033
projected wins
for Democratic candidates

00:00:06.033 --> 00:00:07.267
in Nevada and Arizona,

00:00:07.267 --> 00:00:09.801
defying all the predictions
of a red wave

00:00:09.801 --> 00:00:12.300
and humiliating Republicans,
especially Donald Trump,

00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:14.634
who has been having
a full-blown meltdown

00:00:14.634 --> 00:00:16.834
Now that Republicans are
turning on him and blaming him

00:00:16.834 --> 00:00:18.567
for their party's
catastrophic performance.

00:00:18.567 --> 00:00:20.801
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:20.801 --> 00:00:24.467
♪♪

00:00:24.467 --> 00:00:27.667
I don't have to tell you that
going into these midterms,

00:00:27.667 --> 00:00:29.067
Republicans were very confident.

00:00:29.067 --> 00:00:30.901
They predicted a red wave
that would hand them

00:00:30.901 --> 00:00:33.100
control of both
the House and Senate

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:36.267
and deliver a strong repudiation
of Joe Biden's presidency.

00:00:36.267 --> 00:00:38.801
Some even went further
in predicting a red wave

00:00:38.801 --> 00:00:40.968
and said it would be
much bigger than that.

00:00:40.968 --> 00:00:44.534
-Look, I think we're going
to see a wave election.

00:00:44.534 --> 00:00:45.901
I think it's going
to be a tsunami.

00:00:45.901 --> 00:00:49.000
-Hot just a wave,
but a red tsunami.

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:51.100
-We're not just going
to see a red wave,

00:00:51.100 --> 00:00:52.601
we're going to see
a red tsunami.

00:00:52.601 --> 00:00:55.334
We're not just going
to see a red wave.

00:00:55.334 --> 00:00:57.601
We're going to see a tsunami.

00:00:57.601 --> 00:00:59.434
-[ As Cruz ]
"It won't just be a red wave.

00:00:59.434 --> 00:01:01.000
It'll be a red tsunami.

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:04.701
In fact, it'll be a red monsoon
combined with a red hurricane

00:01:04.701 --> 00:01:07.868
and a red cyclone that hovers
over the Pacific Ocean,

00:01:07.868 --> 00:01:10.701
sucking red sharks
out of the water

00:01:10.701 --> 00:01:12.434
and dumping them
all over America

00:01:12.434 --> 00:01:15.234
in what can only be described
as a red sharknado."

00:01:15.234 --> 00:01:16.567
[ Laughter ]

00:01:16.567 --> 00:01:17.701
[ Normal voice ]
Although I will say,

00:01:17.701 --> 00:01:19.033
Ted Cruz
does have the facial hair

00:01:19.033 --> 00:01:21.133
of a guy who's been stranded
on a desert island

00:01:21.133 --> 00:01:23.934
after getting caught
in a tsunami.

00:01:23.934 --> 00:01:25.968
It looks like he's starring in
a direct-to-video remake

00:01:25.968 --> 00:01:28.334
of "Castaway,"
except in Cruz's version,

00:01:28.334 --> 00:01:30.400
Wilson kills himself
after a week.

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:33.467
[ Laughter ]

00:01:33.467 --> 00:01:36.300
[ As Cruz ]
"I didn't need you, Wilson."

00:01:36.300 --> 00:01:38.133
I got to say, it never gets old
watching Ted Cruz

00:01:38.133 --> 00:01:39.267
get absolutely humiliated.

00:01:39.267 --> 00:01:40.501
The only person who loves it

00:01:40.501 --> 00:01:42.868
more than I do might be,
I don't know, Ted Cruz?

00:01:42.868 --> 00:01:45.868
It's clearly his calling
in life and he's so good at it.

00:01:45.868 --> 00:01:47.601
Donald Trump spent
his entire presidency

00:01:47.601 --> 00:01:49.601
trying to get Congress
to pay for his stupid wall.

00:01:49.601 --> 00:01:51.667
They could have raised
that money in one day

00:01:51.667 --> 00:01:53.834
if they just made Ted Cruz
sit in a dunk tank.

00:01:53.834 --> 00:01:56.934
Do you know how much
they could have brought?

00:01:56.934 --> 00:01:58.701
There would have been
enough money left over

00:01:58.701 --> 00:02:00.334
for a second, smaller wall

00:02:00.334 --> 00:02:02.367
to make sure nobody [bleep]
with the first wall.

00:02:02.367 --> 00:02:03.801
[ Laughter ]

00:02:03.801 --> 00:02:05.133
Anyway, while Cruz

00:02:05.133 --> 00:02:06.801
was confidently
predicting a red tsunami,

00:02:06.801 --> 00:02:09.133
his Senate counterpart,
Florida Senator Rick Scott,

00:02:09.133 --> 00:02:12.968
who was in charge of taking back
the Senate for Republicans,

00:02:12.968 --> 00:02:14.434
was getting even more specific,

00:02:14.434 --> 00:02:16.300
claiming Republicans
could end up with

00:02:16.300 --> 00:02:18.834
as many as 55 seats
after all was said and done,

00:02:18.834 --> 00:02:20.501
and even named specific states

00:02:20.501 --> 00:02:22.467
where he thought Republicans
could upset Democrats.

00:02:22.467 --> 00:02:23.834
-There's every reason to believe

00:02:23.834 --> 00:02:25.934
that we're going to pick up
at least one,

00:02:25.934 --> 00:02:28.801
but I think we can pick up
four or five seats this year.

00:02:28.801 --> 00:02:31.634
If you're Republican,
you want to be a U.S. senator

00:02:31.634 --> 00:02:33.200
and you want to try to change
the direction of the country,

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:34.634
this is the year
you want to run.

00:02:34.634 --> 00:02:36.167
Herschel Walker has already
beaten Warnock

00:02:36.167 --> 00:02:37.567
in Georgia, in the polls.

00:02:37.567 --> 00:02:38.801
Adam Laxalt's already ahead of

00:02:38.801 --> 00:02:41.534
Cortez Masto
by four points in Nevada.

00:02:41.534 --> 00:02:44.000
We will beat Kelly in Arizona.

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:45.901
I think we'll win New Hampshire.

00:02:45.901 --> 00:02:49.167
-Am I crazy to think
that the Republicans could

00:02:49.167 --> 00:02:52.734
win a Senate seat
in Vermont in 2022?

00:02:52.734 --> 00:02:53.734
-You're not crazy.

00:02:53.734 --> 00:02:54.801
-You know, if you really want

00:02:54.801 --> 00:02:56.234
to know
whether or not you're crazy,

00:02:56.234 --> 00:02:59.267
maybe don't ask Rick Scott.

00:02:59.267 --> 00:03:04.267
"If you ask me, all of you
Earth people are crazy."

00:03:04.267 --> 00:03:07.434
[ Laughter ]

00:03:07.434 --> 00:03:09.934
Also, just in general, when you
start a sentence with

00:03:09.934 --> 00:03:13.400
"Am I crazy?" on Fox News,
the answer is almost always yes.

00:03:13.400 --> 00:03:17.133
It would make a great title
for most of their shows.

00:03:17.133 --> 00:03:18.934
Although in fairness,
saying the words "I am crazy"

00:03:18.934 --> 00:03:20.834
is a pretty good indication
that you are,

00:03:20.834 --> 00:03:21.934
no matter where you say it.

00:03:21.934 --> 00:03:23.133
For example, right now there are

00:03:23.133 --> 00:03:24.634
a bunch of Jets fans
sitting around saying,

00:03:24.634 --> 00:03:27.367
"Am I crazy or are we going to
win the Super Bowl this year?"

00:03:27.367 --> 00:03:29.767
And look, the Jets are good.
I'm not denying that.

00:03:29.767 --> 00:03:32.100
But that doesn't mean
they're not still the Jets.

00:03:32.100 --> 00:03:35.734
I said as much to our security
guard, Jim, this morning,

00:03:35.734 --> 00:03:38.033
and then he told me
that NBC has a new policy

00:03:38.033 --> 00:03:41.968
where talent has to
ride to work in the trunk.

00:03:41.968 --> 00:03:43.067
And he also told me "I need to

00:03:43.067 --> 00:03:47.267
keep my [bleep] mouth shut,
desk boy."

00:03:47.267 --> 00:03:49.200
I think he's sensitive

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:51.200
because he already
bought tickets to the Super Bowl

00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:53.367
and the green and white
face paint.

00:03:53.367 --> 00:03:55.467
[ Laughter ]

00:03:55.467 --> 00:03:58.701
Which is an unprofessional thing
to wear to work,

00:03:58.701 --> 00:04:02.267
but obviously...

00:04:02.267 --> 00:04:05.434
[Quietly]
I'm not gonna tell him that!

00:04:05.434 --> 00:04:08.501
Anyway, as you probably
know by now,

00:04:08.501 --> 00:04:10.067
none of those predictions
came true.

00:04:10.067 --> 00:04:12.300
Republicans lost all of those
races except for Georgia,

00:04:12.300 --> 00:04:14.767
where the race will head to
a runoff after Herschel Walker

00:04:14.767 --> 00:04:16.367
finished second
behind Raphael Warnock.

00:04:16.367 --> 00:04:18.501
And now Republicans
have also lost the race

00:04:18.501 --> 00:04:20.634
for control of the Senate
after news organizations

00:04:20.634 --> 00:04:22.300
projected Democratic wins
in the key states

00:04:22.300 --> 00:04:24.968
of Arizona and then Nevada.

00:04:24.968 --> 00:04:26.701
-Fox News alert, the Democrats

00:04:26.701 --> 00:04:29.968
will maintain control
of the Senate.

00:04:29.968 --> 00:04:33.133
The Fox News Decision Desk has
called Nevada's nail-biting

00:04:33.133 --> 00:04:34.534
Senate race in favor of

00:04:34.534 --> 00:04:38.234
incumbent Democrat
Catherine Cortez Masto

00:04:38.234 --> 00:04:41.334
over Republican challenger
Adam Laxalt.

00:04:41.334 --> 00:04:43.067
That gives the Democrats
the 50 seats

00:04:43.067 --> 00:04:46.200
they need to retain
the majority control.

00:04:46.200 --> 00:04:48.801
-What? But the space lizard
and his Sasquatch friend

00:04:48.801 --> 00:04:51.033
told me there
would be a red tsunami.

00:04:51.033 --> 00:04:52.367
[ Laughter ]

00:04:52.367 --> 00:04:54.767
But man, for the news to come
from Fox of all places --

00:04:54.767 --> 00:04:56.367
they're the ones who told us
there'd be a red wave

00:04:56.367 --> 00:04:57.367
in the first place.

00:04:57.367 --> 00:04:58.567
This is like your weatherman

00:04:58.567 --> 00:04:59.767
telling you
it's going to rain all weekend,

00:04:59.767 --> 00:05:02.200
and then after you cancel
all your plans,

00:05:02.200 --> 00:05:04.367
tells you it's actually
75 and sunny,

00:05:04.367 --> 00:05:06.801
so fold up those umbrellas,
or if you don't know how,

00:05:06.801 --> 00:05:11.501
just leave it at the top of the
stairs like an insane person.

00:05:11.501 --> 00:05:15.634
"Am I crazy or can I just
leave this on the steps?"

00:05:15.634 --> 00:05:17.033
You guys remember that?

00:05:17.033 --> 00:05:19.968
That's what we here at
"Late Night" call a classic vid.

00:05:19.968 --> 00:05:22.234
-Classic Vid!

00:05:22.234 --> 00:05:25.434
[ Airhorns sounding ]

00:05:25.434 --> 00:05:30.000
-Do we have to put the stamp
over my face?

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:31.901
The vid's there.

00:05:31.901 --> 00:05:34.133
[ Laughter ]

00:05:34.133 --> 00:05:35.367
Man, I really hope Republicans

00:05:35.367 --> 00:05:36.701
weren't watching Fox News
on Saturday

00:05:36.701 --> 00:05:37.701
when that call happened.

00:05:37.701 --> 00:05:38.734
Of course, that's impossible.

00:05:38.734 --> 00:05:39.834
If you know
any Fox News viewers,

00:05:39.834 --> 00:05:41.267
they're always
watching Fox News.

00:05:41.267 --> 00:05:43.400
One time, I visited my grandma
and the only way to get her

00:05:43.400 --> 00:05:45.968
to stop watching Fox News
was to change her channel

00:05:45.968 --> 00:05:47.701
on her old-ass TV
with a pair of pliers

00:05:47.701 --> 00:05:49.100
and then bury the remote
in the backyard.

00:05:49.100 --> 00:05:50.400
Oh, but she was wily.

00:05:50.400 --> 00:05:51.901
She was out there
all night digging holes,

00:05:51.901 --> 00:05:53.334
looking for that remote.

00:05:53.334 --> 00:05:55.567
When my grandpa saw her
digging a hole out the window

00:05:55.567 --> 00:05:57.434
"in the backyard, he said,
Oh, it's not all bad.

00:05:57.434 --> 00:05:59.334
Now we have someplace
to bury her."

00:05:59.334 --> 00:06:01.767
[ Laughter ]

00:06:01.767 --> 00:06:04.801
That story's not true.

00:06:04.801 --> 00:06:08.000
Every one of my grandparents
is long dead.

00:06:10.901 --> 00:06:12.267
[ Laughter ]

00:06:12.267 --> 00:06:14.767
So Democrats have defied
the odds and defied history

00:06:14.767 --> 00:06:17.067
to produce one of the
best midterm performances

00:06:17.067 --> 00:06:18.767
for the party in power
in political history.

00:06:18.767 --> 00:06:20.901
And now that reality has set in,

00:06:20.901 --> 00:06:23.067
Republicans are furiously
pointing fingers at each other,

00:06:23.067 --> 00:06:24.234
looking for someone to blame.

00:06:24.234 --> 00:06:26.234
And honestly,
it is kind of fun to watch.

00:06:26.234 --> 00:06:28.834
-Donald Trump kept saying,
"We're going to be winning

00:06:28.834 --> 00:06:30.467
so much,
we'll get tired of winning."

00:06:30.467 --> 00:06:32.567
I'm tired of losing.
I mean, that's all he's done.

00:06:32.567 --> 00:06:33.834
-Donald Trump cost us
the president--

00:06:33.834 --> 00:06:36.000
and the Senate twice in a row.

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:38.000
-Our voters didn't show up.
We didn't get the voters.

00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:39.701
It's a complete disappointment.

00:06:39.701 --> 00:06:40.801
-We're not a cult.

00:06:40.801 --> 00:06:42.334
-We're not like, okay,

00:06:42.334 --> 00:06:44.067
there's one person
who leads our party.

00:06:44.067 --> 00:06:47.534
-If the voters conclude
that you're putting your own ego

00:06:47.534 --> 00:06:50.801
or your own grudges ahead
of what's good for the country,

00:06:50.801 --> 00:06:52.133
they're going to look elsewhere.

00:06:52.133 --> 00:06:53.701
-Trump is the past.

00:06:53.701 --> 00:06:56.167
-Let's not vote Mitch McConnell
into leadership.

00:06:56.167 --> 00:06:58.100
He doesn't deserve
to be majority leader

00:06:58.100 --> 00:06:59.534
or minority leader.

00:06:59.534 --> 00:07:02.701
-Josh Hawley tweeted last night,
"The old party is dead.

00:07:02.701 --> 00:07:04.968
Time to bury it.
Build something new."

00:07:04.968 --> 00:07:08.501
-McConnell spent close
to $400 million

00:07:08.501 --> 00:07:10.767
on these Senate candidates.

00:07:10.767 --> 00:07:12.667
I don't know what goes on
behind the scenes,

00:07:12.667 --> 00:07:14.467
but that is a lot of money,

00:07:14.467 --> 00:07:17.400
and we didn't pick up
a single seat?

00:07:17.400 --> 00:07:20.167
So either some of
these candidates are garbage

00:07:20.167 --> 00:07:22.067
or the money's
not being well-spent.

00:07:22.067 --> 00:07:23.634
-Oh, I know. It's both.

00:07:23.634 --> 00:07:26.467
You spend your money poorly
and you spent it on garbage.

00:07:26.467 --> 00:07:28.334
Don't feel bad about it.
We've all done it before.

00:07:28.334 --> 00:07:31.300
Lord knows I've taken an Ambien
and gone on eBay,

00:07:31.300 --> 00:07:33.133
and three days later
I get a package

00:07:33.133 --> 00:07:37.133
with a baseball signed by
Lou Gehrig's friend, Kevin.

00:07:37.133 --> 00:07:38.968
[ Laughter ]

00:07:38.968 --> 00:07:40.901
Ol' sweet Kevin.

00:07:40.901 --> 00:07:43.968
Alabama Congressman Mo Brooks,

00:07:43.968 --> 00:07:45.934
who was once a huge
Trump supporter

00:07:45.934 --> 00:07:47.901
and even spoke at
the Capitol on January 6th

00:07:47.901 --> 00:07:49.734
called Trump
"dishonest, disloyal,

00:07:49.734 --> 00:07:51.801
incompetent and crude,"
which is true,

00:07:51.801 --> 00:07:54.067
but Trump didn't prove
that last week.

00:07:54.067 --> 00:07:56.200
It's just last week,
there were consequences.

00:07:56.200 --> 00:07:58.501
It's like your nephew
telling you today

00:07:58.501 --> 00:08:00.267
he has doubts
about the future of crypto,

00:08:00.267 --> 00:08:01.667
when you definitely remember

00:08:01.667 --> 00:08:04.968
this was his profile picture
last month.

00:08:04.968 --> 00:08:08.501
Really looking forward to seeing
you at Thanksgiving, Kyle.

00:08:08.501 --> 00:08:10.067
I'm guessing this year,
you're not gonna tell me

00:08:10.067 --> 00:08:14.267
it's a shame NBC pays me
in American dollars.

00:08:14.267 --> 00:08:15.567
[ Laughter ]

00:08:15.567 --> 00:08:17.701
Kyle's a lot.

00:08:17.701 --> 00:08:18.968
Still,
it's so great to watch these

00:08:18.968 --> 00:08:20.968
[bleep] turn on each other
like a bunch of roommates

00:08:20.968 --> 00:08:22.601
who got a pet cougar
and now they're all like,

00:08:22.601 --> 00:08:24.534
"Has anyone seen Dave?"

00:08:24.534 --> 00:08:26.434
[ Laughter ]

00:08:26.434 --> 00:08:27.601
Also, just a quick aside,

00:08:27.601 --> 00:08:29.267
my favorite part
of that montage came next,

00:08:29.267 --> 00:08:30.734
when Fox host Jesse Watters

00:08:30.734 --> 00:08:32.634
wondered what happened
to all the money

00:08:32.634 --> 00:08:33.934
Donald Trump raised.

00:08:33.934 --> 00:08:36.400
-Trump's sitting on a massive
war chest in Mar-a-Lago.

00:08:36.400 --> 00:08:39.033
Where'd that money go?
We don't know.

00:08:39.033 --> 00:08:43.834
-No, I think we all know.
It's in his giant coat.

00:08:43.834 --> 00:08:45.567
"Hey, Mr. Trump,
we can't find all the money

00:08:45.567 --> 00:08:46.801
you raised for GOP candidates."

00:08:46.801 --> 00:08:48.234
"Well, best of luck
in your search.

00:08:48.234 --> 00:08:51.133
I'm gonna go out for a walk."

00:08:51.133 --> 00:08:53.067
"In that coat?
It's like, 95 degrees."

00:08:53.067 --> 00:08:54.701
"But the weather can turn.

00:08:54.701 --> 00:08:56.367
So I'm going to keep
the coat on,

00:08:56.367 --> 00:08:58.767
because I misplaced my umbrella
four years ago."

00:08:58.767 --> 00:09:01.634
Now, obviously,
these results have been

00:09:01.634 --> 00:09:02.968
especially
devastating for Trump,

00:09:02.968 --> 00:09:05.367
whose hand-picked
election denier candidates

00:09:05.367 --> 00:09:06.601
lost all across the country.

00:09:06.601 --> 00:09:08.467
And Trump was banking
on a huge sweep

00:09:08.467 --> 00:09:10.133
for his clown car
of bozos and freaks

00:09:10.133 --> 00:09:11.367
so they could help him
win back power.

00:09:11.367 --> 00:09:13.634
Mo Brooks said
earlier this year

00:09:13.634 --> 00:09:16.033
that "Trump had repeatedly
and recently raised the idea

00:09:16.033 --> 00:09:18.133
of attempting to rescind
the 2020 election results

00:09:18.133 --> 00:09:19.467
and reinstall him
as president.

00:09:19.467 --> 00:09:21.501
It was a stunning allegation
that would show Trump

00:09:21.501 --> 00:09:23.467
not only attempted
to subvert the 2020 election

00:09:23.467 --> 00:09:26.234
while in office, but that
he is extracting promises

00:09:26.234 --> 00:09:28.901
from allies to try again
if they take power in 2023."

00:09:28.901 --> 00:09:30.534
Trump actually thought
that was possible.

00:09:30.534 --> 00:09:32.567
How does he think
that would work?

00:09:32.567 --> 00:09:34.501
Does he just think
Congress can pass a bill

00:09:34.501 --> 00:09:37.601
that says Joe Biden has to leave
and then Joe would just do that?

00:09:37.601 --> 00:09:39.534
Because if we have learned
anything about Biden

00:09:39.534 --> 00:09:40.701
from these midterm results,

00:09:40.701 --> 00:09:42.901
it's that he's much savvier
than he appears.

00:09:42.901 --> 00:09:44.634
We said this last week.
We'll say it again.

00:09:44.634 --> 00:09:46.868
Biden's Mr. Magoo bit
where he forgets where he is

00:09:46.868 --> 00:09:50.067
or what he's doing might just be
an act to cover for the fact

00:09:50.067 --> 00:09:51.501
that he's actually
a political mastermind.

00:09:51.501 --> 00:09:52.868
If Trump actually tried
to have Biden

00:09:52.868 --> 00:09:54.601
removed from the White House,
Biden would probably

00:09:54.601 --> 00:09:56.534
do something like pretend
to get stuck on stage

00:09:56.534 --> 00:09:59.767
or, you know, trip on the stairs
three times in a row.

00:09:59.767 --> 00:10:01.200
And then he'd say
something like,

00:10:01.200 --> 00:10:03.000
"Excuse me, Donald,
could you help me up?

00:10:03.000 --> 00:10:04.234
I'm a frail old man."

00:10:04.234 --> 00:10:06.367
And then as soon as Trump
gives his hand to Biden,

00:10:06.367 --> 00:10:07.534
Biden would grab him by the arm

00:10:07.534 --> 00:10:09.167
and just
throw him over his shoulder,

00:10:09.167 --> 00:10:11.434
put him in a headlock and say,
"I'm going to fold you like

00:10:11.434 --> 00:10:13.067
an umbrella, bitch!"

00:10:13.067 --> 00:10:14.934
Now...

00:10:14.934 --> 00:10:16.934
predictably, with
the GOP turning on him,

00:10:16.934 --> 00:10:19.667
Trump is lashing out with
a series of absolutely insane

00:10:19.667 --> 00:10:21.834
and typo-riddled
social media posts.

00:10:21.834 --> 00:10:24.200
Trump has been
attacking fellow Republicans

00:10:24.200 --> 00:10:25.801
like Florida Governor
Ron DeSantis,

00:10:25.801 --> 00:10:27.167
claiming the election
was stolen

00:10:27.167 --> 00:10:29.834
and even insisting that
there should be a do-over.

00:10:29.834 --> 00:10:32.300
-Former President Trump
is already laying

00:10:32.300 --> 00:10:34.200
into Florida Governor
Ron DeSantis,

00:10:34.200 --> 00:10:36.834
as it becomes possible,
the two men may face off

00:10:36.834 --> 00:10:39.033
in a 2024 GOP primary,

00:10:39.033 --> 00:10:42.033
Trump posting to his
Truth Social platform,

00:10:42.033 --> 00:10:45.501
claiming it was he who saved
DeSantis' campaign in 2017

00:10:45.501 --> 00:10:48.968
and accusing him
of lacking loyalty and class.

00:10:48.968 --> 00:10:50.901
-Trump also weighed in
on the midterm results

00:10:50.901 --> 00:10:52.601
on his Truth Social website --

00:10:52.601 --> 00:10:55.200
in one post, he claimed New
Hampshire's Republican

00:10:55.200 --> 00:10:57.567
Senate nominee lost his race

00:10:57.567 --> 00:11:01.133
for not staying strong
and true about the Big Lie.

00:11:01.133 --> 00:11:02.901
-He said that because Arizona
is likely to

00:11:02.901 --> 00:11:04.367
still be counting
at the end of the week,

00:11:04.367 --> 00:11:07.167
that must mean they want
more time to cheat.

00:11:07.167 --> 00:11:10.033
-Trump took to
Truth Social with a tirade,

00:11:10.033 --> 00:11:11.167
writing in part,

00:11:11.167 --> 00:11:15.400
"They stole the electron
from Blake Masters."

00:11:15.400 --> 00:11:19.400
He he wrote the word "electron,"
as in a subatomic particle.

00:11:19.400 --> 00:11:21.834
Adding,
"Do election over again!"

00:11:21.834 --> 00:11:23.234
Exclamation point.

00:11:23.234 --> 00:11:24.767
-How is it possible
that he typed

00:11:24.767 --> 00:11:26.734
"electron" instead of
"election"?

00:11:26.734 --> 00:11:28.501
I would say that maybe
Trump got screwed

00:11:28.501 --> 00:11:31.934
by autocorrect on that one,
but then, is it really possible

00:11:31.934 --> 00:11:35.033
that Trump's autocorrect hasn't
learned the word "election"?

00:11:35.033 --> 00:11:37.634
It's literally all
he tweets about --

00:11:37.634 --> 00:11:40.400
not tweets, whatever they
call them on Truth Social --

00:11:40.400 --> 00:11:42.400
bloops, bleeps, derps?

00:11:42.400 --> 00:11:44.200
May I suggest brain farts?

00:11:44.200 --> 00:11:47.400
I think that would be better
than saying "a post."

00:11:47.400 --> 00:11:48.868
Just imagine Wolf Blitzer
saying,

00:11:48.868 --> 00:11:49.901
"The former president

00:11:49.901 --> 00:11:51.901
with a new brain fart
on Truth Social,

00:11:51.901 --> 00:11:55.267
claiming the electron
has been rigged."

00:11:55.267 --> 00:11:57.734
Whatever, I'm shocked Trump
is capable of

00:11:57.734 --> 00:11:59.634
spelling the word
"electron" even by accident,

00:11:59.634 --> 00:12:01.200
since there's no way
he knows what it is.

00:12:01.200 --> 00:12:02.367
"We all love --

00:12:02.367 --> 00:12:04.300
We all love electron,
don't we, folks?

00:12:04.300 --> 00:12:06.567
He's the bad guy
from the Avengers movies, right?

00:12:06.567 --> 00:12:08.367
'The Rise of Electron.'

00:12:08.367 --> 00:12:11.133
One of my favorite of all --
of all the ages,

00:12:11.133 --> 00:12:13.334
was the Age of Electron."

00:12:13.334 --> 00:12:14.968
Trump is reportedly
on the verge of announcing

00:12:14.968 --> 00:12:16.834
that he'll run for president
again in 2024,

00:12:16.834 --> 00:12:18.367
but Republicans are
already turning on him

00:12:18.367 --> 00:12:19.634
and turning on each other.

00:12:19.634 --> 00:12:22.467
Voters rejected Trumpism
and the MAGA movement yet again,

00:12:22.467 --> 00:12:24.834
just as they did
in 2018 and 2020,

00:12:24.834 --> 00:12:26.834
and now Democrats
have defied history

00:12:26.834 --> 00:12:29.701
and will control the Senate for
the rest of Biden's first term.

00:12:29.701 --> 00:12:32.033
Trump is probably at home right
now trying to psych himself up,

00:12:32.033 --> 00:12:34.367
staring in the mirror, telling
himself over and over again...

00:12:34.367 --> 00:12:35.667
-You're not crazy.

00:12:35.667 --> 00:12:37.667
This has been "A Closer Look."

00:12:37.667 --> 00:12:41.467
♪♪

